  "label": "Anti-Black Stereotype",
  "description": "The meme's framing, particularly the text 'how slaves were mistreated,' may implicitly reinforce or evoke harmful anti-Black stereotypes by reducing the complex, systemic trauma of slavery to a sensationalized, simplistic visual narrative. This can perpetuate the idea that enslaved people were inherently passive or submissive, ignoring their resistance, agency, and humanity. The image may also be used to reinforce the stereotype that Black people are inherently prone to violence or suffering, which is a distortion of historical reality.",
